and the business is down 17%,

00:13:08.554 --> 00:13:11.958
is way too often, and
somehow we accept that.

00:13:11.958 --> 00:13:13.459
So, I think we have 
to have a far more

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:15.495
serious conversation 
around measurement,

00:13:15.495 --> 00:13:17.730
because we're measuring 
the wrong things.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.966
This is, we are 
absolutely somehow

00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:23.536
eliminating common
sense from the equation.

00:13:25.705 --> 00:13:26.906
And there was a lot, 
I mean there's,

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:28.408
I just think it's
fundamentally fascinating.

00:13:28.408 --> 00:13:30.043
I mean, I don't think 
agencies are built

00:13:30.043 --> 00:13:31.978
to have aligned interests
with their clients,

00:13:31.978 --> 00:13:34.147
which is why you 
get into weird tactics.

00:13:34.147 --> 00:13:36.349
I think there's hidden
costs in production,

00:13:36.349 --> 00:13:38.584
which is ludicrous, 
I mean, I don't know.

00:13:38.584 --> 00:13:39.952
I think the whole 
thing is fasc--

00:13:39.952 --> 00:13:41.621
I don't think it's, 
but wait, who am I?

00:13:41.621 --> 00:13:45.191
I'm one dude, I just think
that, I just think that

00:13:45.191 --> 00:13:47.260
it's a very interesting
ecosystem.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.461
Like, I went to a meeting where

00:13:48.461 --> 00:13:50.630
the first presentation 
was by a PR company

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:53.933
that claimed that some 
mention in Huff Po

00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:57.603
14 pages into 
their website attributes

00:13:57.603 --> 00:13:59.839
80 million impressions 
for the month,

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:01.808
I mean like, we're just
playing weird games.

00:14:01.808 --> 00:14:04.677
I think we're, we're just
eliminating common sense,

00:14:04.677 --> 00:14:06.746
and I think that's 
a huge mistake.

00:14:06.746 --> 00:14:08.715
- Yeah, I think metrics is
a great thing to talk about

00:14:08.715 --> 00:14:10.016
in terms of that, so
what, in terms of what

00:14:10.016 --> 00:14:11.984
you're focused on when you
present to your clients,

00:14:11.984 --> 00:14:14.087
I'm sure they still expect
you to present a report

00:14:14.087 --> 00:14:15.621
of the traditional metrics.
- Oh, we do tons--

00:14:15.621 --> 00:14:17.390
- So what do you show?
- of horseshit stuff.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.092
We, we--
(laughing)

00:14:19.092 --> 00:14:21.828
We do a ton of horse shit 
stuff because we,

00:14:21.828 --> 00:14:24.731
they force us to 
after this conversation.

00:14:24.731 --> 00:14:28.768
We say to them, 
we want to measure sales,

00:14:28.768 --> 00:14:31.471
you know, we wanna 
measure the thing,

00:14:31.471 --> 00:14:34.006
donations, like, the thing.

00:14:34.006 --> 00:14:35.675
Like TV clients, Neilsen ratings

00:14:35.675 --> 00:14:37.744
'cause that's your
currency you make money on.

00:14:37.744 --> 00:14:40.346
Like, we wanna 
measure the thing,

00:14:40.346 --> 00:14:42.548
the problem is, 
99% of our clients

00:14:42.548 --> 00:14:46.385
do not put us in a position
to measure the thing.

00:14:46.385 --> 00:14:47.787
Which gets me 
into like, why doesn't

00:14:47.787 --> 00:14:49.222
anybody wanna measure the thing?

00:14:49.222 --> 00:14:50.156
(laughing)
Right?

00:14:50.156 --> 00:14:52.325
Like, like I think nobody
wants to be held accountable.

00:14:52.325 --> 00:14:55.228
I think one of the great
things about Corporate America

00:14:55.228 --> 00:14:57.663
and agency landscape that
I didn't understand was,

00:14:57.663 --> 00:14:59.532
I used to be mad at everybody.

00:14:59.532 --> 00:15:02.535
Mad that you didn't care
enough to do the right thing.

00:15:02.535 --> 00:15:04.504
Then what I realized is,
I can't be mad at you,

00:15:04.504 --> 00:15:06.239
the game is structured in a way

00:15:06.239 --> 00:15:07.907
that people are
playing within it,

00:15:07.907 --> 00:15:09.642
because you have 
mortgages, and a family,

00:15:09.642 --> 00:15:11.310
and like, you're just,
you're making decisions

00:15:11.310 --> 00:15:14.514
